ust help
Command-line tools for working with a log of user stories.

User stories are stored as Markdown files in the project's `docs/userstory`
directory.  Each story's file name begins with `STORY-` and its number, such
as `STORY-0001-describe-work-in-user-stories.md`.  Run "ust init" to start a
log, and "ust new" to add to it.

Usage:
  ust [flags]
  ust [command]

Available Commands:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  config      Print the configuration in use
  graph       Draw the links between records in Mermaid or Graphviz format
  help        Help about any command
  init        Start a log of user stories
  link        Record that one user story replaces or updates another
  list        List the user stories, or write a table of contents
  new         Create the next numbered user story

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for ust

Use "ust [command] --help" for more information about a command.
ust help new
Creates a new, numbered user story, in draft.  The title is a single argument,
so it must be quoted if it contains spaces.  The story is opened for editing in
the editor specified by the VISUAL or EDITOR environment variable (VISUAL is
preferred; EDITOR is used if VISUAL is not set).  After editing, the file name
of the story is output to stdout, so the command can be used in scripts.

If the story directory contains a file `templates/template.md`, this is used
as the template for the new story.  Otherwise a built-in template is used, with
sections for the story, its acceptance criteria and notes, in the form
described by Mike Cohn in this guide:

  https://www.mountaingoatsoftware.com/agile/user-stories

Multiple --replace and --update options can be given, so that the new story
can replace or update multiple existing stories.  A replaced story loses its
Draft status; an updated one keeps its status.

Usage:
  ust new TITLE [flags]

Examples:
  # Create a new story with the title "Export invoices for a month":
  ust new "Export invoices for a month"

  # Split story 4 in two, replacing it with two smaller stories:
  ust new -r 4 "Reorder a previous purchase"
  ust new -r 4 "Adjust quantities when reordering"

  # Create a new story that updates story 7:
  ust new -u 7 "Warn of clashing sessions"

Flags:
  -h, --help                help for new
  -r, --replace REFERENCE   a REFERENCE (number or partial filename) to a record this one replaces
  -u, --update REFERENCE    a REFERENCE (number or partial filename) to a record this one updates
ust help link
Records, in both stories, that SOURCE replaces or updates TARGET.

SOURCE and TARGET are both a reference (number or partial filename) to a user
story.  Exactly one of --replace and --update must be given.

With --replace, SOURCE replaces TARGET, which is marked "Replaced by" SOURCE
and loses its Draft status.  When a story is split, each of the smaller
stories replaces it.

With --update, SOURCE makes substantive changes to TARGET, which is marked
"Updated by" SOURCE and keeps its status.

Usage:
  ust link (--replace | --update) SOURCE TARGET [flags]

Examples:
  # Record that story 3 updates story 2:
  ust link --update 3 2

  # Record that stories 11 and 12 replace story 10, which was split:
  ust link -r 11 10
  ust link -r 12 10

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for link
  -r, --replace   SOURCE replaces TARGET, which loses its Draft status
  -u, --update    SOURCE makes substantive changes to TARGET
ust nonsense
ust: unknown command "nonsense" for "ust"
